//
//  Himalia firmware -- wavetable version
//
//  The sample player is replaced by a wavetable oscillator on SAMPLE OUT:
//   - SAMPLE TUNE knob + CV ....... pitch (exponential)
//   - SAMPLE SELECT knob + CV ..... scan / morph through the waves of a table
//   - RATCHET knob + CV ........... wavetable select
//   - A/B button (sample side) .... wavefolder on / off   (LPG mode: short / long decay)
//   - TRIGGER in / button ......... phase reset (sync), LED flashes
//   - BIT switch .................. LPG mode: the wavetable goes through a
//                                   low pass gate (vactrol style) that opens on
//                                   trigger / gate. Replaces the 8 bit bytebeat mode.
//  Wavetables come from wavetables.h, made by tools/make_wavetables.py
//  (your own Serum/Vital style wav files + built-in tables).
//
//  The 6 squares are a generative sequencer (Turing machine style):
//   - clock: SAMPLE TRIGGER in / button, every trigger is one step
//   - SQUARES MAIN TUNE knob + CV ... root pitch
//   - SPREAD knob + CV .............. change: left = loop locked, right = random
//   - A/B button (squares side) ..... scale: A = minor pentatonic, B = natural minor
//   - 6 voices: melody, sub octave, two harmonies, octave up, drone; the register
//     decides per step which voices sound, their pulse width and filter cap
//
//  The digital noise / S&H is a stereo ping-pong delay on the wavetable:
//   - left = SAMPLE OUT (dry + echoes), right = noise side DAC out (echoes)
//   - time = time between triggers x division
//   - CLOCK RATE knob: division 1/8 1/6 1/4 1/3 3/8 1/2 2/3 3/4 1 4/3 3/2 2
//   - CV IN RATE: feedback (unpatched 45%)
//   - rate LED + PA22: pulse on every echo time
//
//  Other changes against the factory firmware:
//   - linker scripts use the full 1 MB flash of the ATSAMD51J20A
//   - unused libraries removed (Wire, SdFat, Adafruit_SPIFlash)
//   - hysteresis on the spread selector
//   - sample tune jack: correct pin (PB06) is switched to analog mode
//
